      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיק</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵק</span></big>  <strong>substantivo.</strong>[<strong>masculino.</strong>] <strong>seio (</strong>hebraico pós-bíblico <em>idem.</em><strong>)</strong>—absoluto <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיק</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.17\">Ez 43:17</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 16:33\" href=\"/Proverbs.16.33\">Pr 16:33</a> + <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.13\">Ez 43:13</a> (Co <span dir=\"rtl\">חיקו</span>, cf. ZKW <sup>1883, pp. 67 ff.</sup>; <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיקֹה</span> Dr<sup>Sm xxxi</sup>), <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵק</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 21:14\" href=\"/Proverbs.21.14\">Pr 21:14</a>; construto <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיק</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:35\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.35\">1 K 22:35</a> + 3 vezes + <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.14\">Ez 43:14</a> (Co <span dir=\"rtl\">חיקו</span>) <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵק</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.20\">Pr 5:20</a> (omitido acidentalmente em Baer, cf. Str<sup>ad loc.</sup>) <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:23\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.23\">17:23</a>; com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיקִי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 3:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.3.20\">1 K 3:20</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 89:51\" href=\"/Psalms.89.51\">ψ 89:51</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵקִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 19:27\" href=\"/Job.19.27\">Jb 19:27</a> etc.; nas demais passagens sempre escrito plene com sufixo; <span dir=\"rtl\">חוקך</span> Ketib <a data-ref=\"Psalms 74:11\" href=\"/Psalms.74.11\">ψ 74:11</a> (Qere <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיקְךָ</span>);—<em>seio</em>, especificamente.<br><strong>1.</strong>  da dobra da veste, junto ao peito <a data-ref=\"Exodus 4:6\" href=\"/Exodus.4.6\">Ex 4:6</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 4:7\" href=\"/Exodus.4.7\">7</a><sup>(×3)</sup> (todos J), <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:27\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.27\">Pr 6:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 16:33\" href=\"/Proverbs.16.33\">16:33</a>, metáfora de <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 74:11\" href=\"/Psalms.74.11\">ψ 74:11</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁחַד בח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 21:14\" href=\"/Proverbs.21.14\">Pr 21:14</a> é uma <em>recompensa oculta</em> (escondida no seio; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מַתָּן בַּסֵּתֶר</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁחַד מֵחֵק</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:23\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.23\">17:23</a> é um <em>presente dado em segredo;</em> figurado, <em>retribuir no seio</em> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 65:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.65.6\">Is 65:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 65:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.65.7\">7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:18\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.18\">Je 32:18</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 35:13\" href=\"/Psalms.35.13\">ψ 35:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 79:12\" href=\"/Psalms.79.12\">79:12</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>carregar</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">(נָשָׁא)</span> <em>no colo</em>, Moisés o povo <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:12\" href=\"/Numbers.11.12\">Nu 11:12</a> (JE); Noemi, o filho de Rute <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:16\" href=\"/Ruth.4.16\">Ru 4:16</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 3:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.3.20\">1 K 3:20</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 17:19\" href=\"/I_Kings.17.19\">17:19</a>; cordeirinha <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 12:3\" href=\"/II_Samuel.12.3\">2 S 12:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 40:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.40.11\">Is 40:11</a> (metáfora); <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:12\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.12\">La 2:12</a> de crianças morrendo nos braços de suas mães; figura de levar insultos no próprio seio <a data-ref=\"Psalms 89:51\" href=\"/Psalms.89.51\">ψ 89:51</a> (ler provavelmente <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּלִמַּת</span> por <span dir=\"rtl\">כֹּל</span>, ver Bi Che).<br><strong>3.</strong>  <em>seio</em> como parte do corpo: <strong>a.</strong>  externo, <em>jazer no seio</em>, da esposa <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁכבת</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:5\" href=\"/Micah.7.5\">Mi 7:5</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 12:8\" href=\"/II_Samuel.12.8\">2 S 12:8</a>; concubina <a data-ref=\"Genesis 16:5\" href=\"/Genesis.16.5\">Gn 16:5</a> (J) cf. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 1:2\" href=\"/I_Kings.1.2\">1 K 1:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵשֶׁת חיק(ך)</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 13:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.13.7\">Dt 13:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:54\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.54\">28:54</a>, cf. também <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.20\">Pr 5:20</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּחַבֵּק חֵק נָכְרִיָּה</span>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אִישׁ חֵיקָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:56\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.56\">Dt 28:56</a>. <strong>b.</strong>  interno, a ira repousa <span dir=\"rtl\">בח׳ כסילים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 7:9\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.7.9\">Ec 7:9</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּלוּ כִלְיֹתַי בְּחֵקִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 19:27\" href=\"/Job.19.27\">Jb 19:27</a> <em>meus rins se consomem dentro de mim;</em> <a data-ref=\"Job 23:12\" href=\"/Job.23.12\">Jb 23:12</a> (ler <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּחֵקִי</span> por <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵחֻקִּי</span>, assim 𝔊 𝔙 Ol Me Stu Di) <em>em meu peito escondi as palavras de sua boca</em> (cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּלִבִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:11\" href=\"/Psalms.119.11\">ψ 119:11</a>); figura do interior de carro <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:35\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.35\">1 K 22:35</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ח׳ הרכב</span>; do fundo côncavo do altar <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.13\">Ez 43:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.14\">14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.17\">17</a> (Sm <em>canaleta (Rinne);</em> Co <em>moldura da base (Grundeinfassung)</em>).",
